    "description": "Altán Redes operates Mexico's shared wholesale mobile network, Red Compartida. Its customers are mobile network operators, MVNOs, enterprises, and public-sector users that buy wholesale capacity rather than retail subscribers, and the business runs an asset-heavy national wireless infrastructure platform. Public company and government sources describe the network as a 4.5G LTE wholesale system with population coverage above 94% as of mid-2024, although other later public reports cite lower figures using different measures. Altán was created to deploy and operate the Red Compartida under a long-term public-private partnership and received its concession in 2017. Morgan Stanley Infrastructure Partners publicly lists Altán as a portfolio investment from March 2017, but reviewed sources also show a later government-led financial restructuring and state participation. Because the current sponsor-level ownership structure after that restructuring is not clearly disclosed in the public sources reviewed, ownership details are recorded as not publicly disclosed.",
